INSERT INTO `mst_objective` VALUES ('AI01.M27','Identify Automated Solutions','Analysing business requirements and specifying feasible automated solutions to meet business needs.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI02.M27','Acquire and Maintain Application Software','Applications are made available in line with business requirements through custom development or acquisition.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI03.M27','Acquire and Maintain Technology Infrastructure','Providing suitable hardware, system software and network infrastructure to support business applications.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI04.M27','Enable Operation and Use','Providing documentation, user manuals and training materials to enable proper operation and use of applications.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI05.M27','Procure IT Resources','Improving IT resource acquisition through proper vendor evaluation, contracting and procurement processes.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI06.M27','Manage Changes','All changes to information systems and infrastructure are assessed, approved and implemented in a controlled manner.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('AI07.M27','Install and Accredit Solutions and Changes','Testing and accreditation of new systems and changes prior to release into production operations.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS01.M27','Define and Manage Service Levels','Communication between IT and customers is maintained through formal service level agreements (SLAs).','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS02.M27','Manage Third-party Services','Establishing relationships with external service providers and monitoring vendor service delivery.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS03.M27','Manage Performance and Capacity','Ensuring IT capacity and resources are sufficient to satisfy current and future service requirements.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS04.M27','Ensure Continuous Service','Developing IT continuity plans to ensure resilience and recovery in the event of major disruptions.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS05.M27','Ensure Systems Security','Maintaining the integrity of information and protection of IT assets against unauthorised access.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS06.M27','Identify and Allocate Costs','A fair and equitable system of identifying and allocating IT costs to business users.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS07.M27','Educate and Train Users','Organising structured training and education for users to maximise effective and secure use of IT systems.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS08.M27','Manage Service Desk and Incidents','Timely and effective response to user queries, problems and incident resolution via service desk.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS09.M27','Manage the Configuration','Maintaining accurate records of configuration items (CIs) and relationships across IT infrastructure.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS10.M27','Manage Problems','Identifying root causes of incidents and preventing recurrence of IT service disruptions.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS11.M27','Manage Data','Ensuring that data remains complete, accurate and valid throughout its lifecycle and backup operations.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS12.M27','Manage the Physical Environment','Providing physical security and environmental protection for computer facilities against physical threats.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('DS13.M27','Manage Operations','Ensuring that daily operational tasks, job scheduling and system maintenance are carried out reliably.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('ME01.M27','Monitor and Evaluate IT Performance','Establishing an IT performance monitoring framework and periodic reporting against goals.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('ME02.M27','Monitor and Evaluate Internal Control','Assessing the effectiveness of the internal control environment for IT operations and governance.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('ME03.M27','Ensure Regulatory Compliance','Ensuring compliance of IT processes with applicable laws, statutory, and contractual requirements.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('ME04.M27','Provide IT Governance','Establishing an effective governance framework aligned with COBIT principles and board oversight.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO01.M27','Define a Strategic IT Plan','IT strategic planning is required to manage and direct all IT resources in line with the business strategy and priorities. The IT function and business stakeholders are responsible for ensuring that optimal value is realised from project and service portfolios. The strategic plan improves key stakeholders\' understanding of IT opportunities and limitations, assesses current performance, identifies capacity and human resource requirements, and clarifies the level of investment required. The business strategy and priorities are to be reflected in portfolios and executed by the IT tactical plan(s), which specifies concise objectives, action plans and tasks that are understood and accepted by both business and IT.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO02.M27','Define the Information Architecture','The information systems function creates and regularly updates a business information model and defines the appropriate systems to optimise the use of this information. This encompasses the development of a corporate data dictionary with the organisation\'s data syntax rules, data classification scheme and security levels. This process improves the quality of management decision making by making sure that reliable and secure information is provided, and it enables rationalising information systems resources to appropriately match business strategies. This IT process is also needed to increase accountability for the integrity and security of data and to enhance the effectiveness and control of sharing information across applications and entities.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO03.M27','Determine Technological Direction','tes 3 ee','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO04.M27','Define the IT Processes, Organisation and Relationships','An IT organisation is established by considering requirements for staff, skills, functions, authorities, roles and responsibilities.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO05.M27','Manage the IT Investment','Establishing and maintaining a budgeting and accounting process to manage and monitor IT investment and spending.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO06.M27','Communicate Management Aims and Direction','Management develops an enterprise control environment and communicates management direction.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO07.M27','Manage IT Human Resources','Acquiring, maintaining and motivating a competent workforce for the creation and delivery of IT services.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO08.M27','Manage Quality','A quality management system (QMS) is established and maintained to ensure continuous quality improvement.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO09.M27','Assess and Manage IT Risks','A risk management framework is created and maintained to identify, evaluate and manage IT-related risks.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO10.M27','Manage Projects','Establishing a programme and project management framework for IT projects to deliver within scope, budget and time.','COBIT 4.1 Control Objectives and Management Guidelines',27),('PO2.M27','Define the Information Architecture','The information systems function creates and regularly updates a business information model and defines the appropriate systems to optimise the use of this information. This encompasses the development of a corporate data dictionary with the organisation’s data syntax rules, data classification scheme and security levels. This process improves the quality of management decision making by making sure that reliable and secure information is provided, and it enables rationalising information systems resources to appropriately match business strategies. This IT process is also needed to increase accountability for the integrity and security of data and to enhance the effectiveness and control of sharing information across applications and entities.',NULL,27);
